Q1. Store and Display Personal Information
Question:
Write a program to store a person's name, age, height, and city in variables and display all the information.

Sample Input:
Name: Rahul
Age: 22
Height: 5.8
City: Meerut


Expected Output:
Name: Rahul
Age: 22
Height: 5.8
City: Meerut


Python Code:
name = "Rahul"age = 22height = 5.8city = "Meerut"print("Name:", name)print("Age:", age)print("Height:", height)print("City:", city)



C Code:
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    char name[] = "Rahul";
    int age = 22;
    float height = 5.8;
    char city[] = "Meerut";

    printf("Name: %s\n", name);
    printf("Age: %d\n", age);
    printf("Height: %.1f\n", height);
    printf("City: %s\n", city);

    return 0;
}


Java Code:
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String name = "Rahul";
        int age = 22;
        float height = 5.8f;
        String city = "Meerut";

        System.out.println("Name: " + name);
        System.out.println("Age: " + age);
        System.out.println("Height: " + height);
        System.out.println("City: " + city);
    }
}



Q2. Perform Basic Arithmetic Operations
Question:
Write a program to store two numbers in variables and perform addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, and modulus operations.

Sample Input:
First Number: 20
Second Number: 6


Expected Output:
Addition: 26
Subtraction: 14
Multiplication: 120
Division: 3.333333
Modulus: 2


Python Code:
a = 20b = 6print("Addition:", a + b)print("Subtraction:", a - b)print("Multiplication:", a * b)print("Division:", a / b)print("Modulus:", a % b)



C Code:
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int a = 20;
    int b = 6;

    printf("Addition: %d\n", a + b);
    printf("Subtraction: %d\n", a - b);
    printf("Multiplication: %d\n", a * b);
    printf("Division: %.6f\n", (float)a / b);
    printf("Modulus: %d\n", a % b);

    return 0;
